%N A397249 Numbers m such that lambda(2^m - 1) + 1 is prime, where the Carmichael lambda function is A002322.
%C A397249 Numbers m such that A387107(m) + 1 is prime. Are there infinitely many such m?
%C A397249 It contains, among others, all Mersenne primes (A000668) and all Fermat primes (A019434).
%C A397249 In the above sequence, some prime repeat in pairs. Are there only finitely many such doubles?
%H A397249 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A397249/b397249.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..81</a>
%F A397249 A387107(a(n)) + 1 >= A005420(a(n)) for n >= 2.
%t A397249 q[m_] := PrimeQ[CarmichaelLambda[2^m-1] + 1]; Select[Range[100], q] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 21 2026 *)
%Y A397249 Cf. A000043 (subsequence), A000225, A000668, A002322 (lambda), A019434, A092506, A387107 (lambda(2^n-1)).
%K A397249 nonn,new
%O A397249 1,2
